{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310542,"nonce":"VboOyzG0Fxwlluq5Tk0P/XwuRr4=","title":"Same-build BLADE mixed-cache bugs (fresh-vs-cached modules) — layer 1 (append bare-extern panic) FIXED; layers remain. Full F1-F9 fix plan ...","message":"**Context (2026-06-12):** cross-BUILD cache staleness was fixed via\nbuild-id rerun coverage, but a 5-scenario matrix exposed SAME-build\nmixed-cache bugs: A fresh-all ✓; B full-warm \"works\" while replaying\n~19 stored IMPORT errors; C touch-entry-only = FATAL `can't resolve\nsymbol append` Cranelift panic; D/E edit-a-dep = fatal. Scenario C is\nthe everyday dev loop. The bug even ate its own diagnostics twice\n(benches/A-B tests run in mixed state after any source revert).\n\n**Fixed (layer 1, committed):** `try_load_import_from_cache` never\npopulated `import_own_func_ids` → cached user-module methods\nunprotected at stdlib merge → bare-extern fallthrough → JIT finalize\npanic / AOT undefined symbol. Fix mirrors fresh path, scoped STRICTLY\nto declared functions via `cached_maps.functions`. **Scoping lesson:**\nmarking all non-empty-CFG functions also protects generated stdlib\nwrapper placeholders inside user modules → they shadow real stdlib MIR\n→ cached StringMap.get dispatches into a stub (\"missing meta key\n'general.architecture'\", GGUF load hangs) — strictly worse than the\noriginal bug.\n\n**Deferred with reason:** F4 (skip Main.mir.cache write when compile\nhas Error diagnostics) — implemented, then reverted to a TODO at the\nsave site (src/main.rs ~1639): TODAY a normal successful build of\nllama-chat-server silently stores ~19 error diagnostics (the F8 latent\nbugs), so gating on errors disables the warm path entirely and forces\nevery run into the still-broken mixed state.\n\n**Progress 2026-06-12 late session:** F8a LANDED — abstract member\npre-pass (symbols + signature types before body lowering, mirroring the\nclass pre-pass) killed the IMPORT storm at the source: 19 → 8 stored\nerrors, ZERO printed on fresh compile, 132/133 suite, Paris ✓. Replay\nfilter LANDED — warm runs no longer replay error-severity strings from\nthe producing compile (RAYZOR_REPLAY_CACHED_ERRORS=1 reverts), so\nfresh + warm + warm-again all print zero errors. F4 re-attempted and\nre-deferred: 8 silent stored errors remain in three classes (exact list\nin the F4 TODO in src/main.rs): Int32 'Invalid assignment target' ×4\n(abstract op-assign), Int64.high/low receiver-property (SECOND E0100\nemitter ~hir_to_mir.rs:26514 — the instrumented one at :26203 is fixed),\nMath POSITIVE/NEGATIVE_INFINITY extern statics (F8b). Probes:\nRAYZOR_DUMP_STORED_DIAGS=1, RAYZOR_E0100_DEBUG=1.\n\n**Remaining plan (workflow wf_1908da0f-d42 synthesis, full text in its\noutput file):**\n- F5 dependency-closure invalidation — blade metadata already saves\n  `dependencies`; resolve via bare_to_qualified, session dirty-set,\n  treat as miss when any dep changed. THE soundness fix for D/E.\n- F7 diagnostics visibility — fresh compiles render errors to the\n  cache blob but don't PRINT them; B's \"19 errors\" are A's silent\n  errors replayed. Surface at compile time.\n- F8 latent compiler bugs behind the 19 (fire on every fresh build):\n  (a) abstract member pre-registration (Int32.clamp, Int64.high — no\n  pre_register pass for abstracts in ast_lowering); (b) extern-only\n  stdlib statics as MIR globals (Math.PI/NaN/INFINITY — NO e2E TEST\n  EXISTS for Math.PI, why 128/128 stays green); (c) save blades from\n  the on-demand loader (KvCacheQ8 recompiles every run); (d) retry-pass\n  stale-snapshot truncate (doubled diagnostics).\n- F2 don't mint bare-name extern stubs when a plugin maps the method\n  (KvCacheQ8.append → rayzor_kv_cache_q8_append); F3 hard error at\n  cranelift declare instead of finalize panic (no-silent-fallthrough).\n- F6 signature_hash check on the primary fixup path (only the bare-name\n  fallback checks today).\n\n**Regression gate:** the 5-scenario matrix (fresh / warm / touch-entry\n/ edit-mid-dep / edit-deep-dep, each run TWICE for poison persistence)\n+ 128 suite + Paris canonical + new tests (Math.PI read, abstract\nforward-ref member, user-method vs stdlib bare-name collision).\n\n**GROUNDED UPDATE 2026-06-14 (session 2, workflow wf_7c0ea216-38a):**\n- **F5 is effectively DONE** by commit a652c88. It folded\n  `compute_import_set_hash` into `hash_source_for_config`\n  (compilation.rs:755), and BOTH the entry cache AND the per-module cache\n  (`try_load_blade_cached_full`, compilation.rs:3333) validate against\n  `hash_source_for_config`. So a module's per-module `native/*.blade`\n  cache now invalidates when ANY file in its transitive import closure\n  changes content. (An earlier investigator claimed per-module caches\n  ignore deps — that was the PRE-a652c88 behavior; the shared\n  `hash_source_for_config` covers them.) Verified: dep edit → cache MISS\n  → recompile (0.16s hit → 0.83s on a real dep edit).\n- **The \"Warning→fatal move-ERROR\" escalation is a RED HERRING / not\n  reproducible.** Move detection (compilation.rs `check_ownership_violations`\n  ~6650, `check_use_after_move`) is purely INTRA-procedural and reads no\n  cross-module callee signature. Warning→Error needs the var type to be a\n  `@:move` class (compilation.rs:6465); there are ZERO `@:move` classes\n  (Tensor/QTensor are `@:shared` → skipped; `String` is primitive TypeId 4\n  → always Warning). My earlier \"value used here after move FATAL\" sighting\n  did not reproduce on a clean-binary repro — likely a stale-binary\n  confound. Do NOT chase the ownership checker.\n- **The real residual is F6, NOT F5:** with F5 done, editing one dep\n  (e.g. GenerationLoop.hx) correctly recompiles that module + the entry\n  while leaving UNRELATED modules (BPETokenizer, GGUFReader) cached — they\n  don't depend on the edit, so their caches are valid. The failure is the\n  cached module's CROSS-MODULE refs (function ids / interface vtable\n  indices) being stale relative to the freshly-renumbered modules →\n  runtime **SIGSEGV (exit 139)** at GGUF load (non-deterministic across\n  which file is edited: SIGSEGV / wrong-key). The fix is making\n  `fixup_stale_cross_module_refs` + the `signature_hash` check (F6) cover\n  the cached-module → fresh-module direction, OR (coarse, sound, loses\n  incremental) force a full recompile whenever the entry import-set hash\n  changes (fold the ENTRY's compilation-wide dep hash into every module's\n  key so any change invalidates all module caches).\n- **NEXT (low-risk first step):** instrument `try_load_import_from_cache`\n  (compilation.rs ~3228) to log per-module hit/miss for the llama-chat\n  graph after a dep edit; pinpoint which cached module replays the stale\n  ref that segfaults; that names the exact F6 target. THIS SUBSYSTEM IS\n  DANGEROUS (it ate its own diagnostics twice; F4/F8 deferrals) — do F6\n  in a focused session with the full 5-scenario regression matrix, not\n  rushed.\n\n**UPDATE 2026-06-23 — `test_balancedtree_crossmodule_mono` suite failure is a CUMULATIVE-CACHE flake, NOT a clean regression.** It FAILS in the full `run_haxe_tests.sh` (151 tests share ONE `.rayzor` cache, runner uses cache-on no `--no-cache`) — error `EnumValueMap failed to compile: Cannot find name 'root' (67:17)` (the bare inherited `root` in `EnumValueMap.copy()`, from `BalancedTree`), then exit 138 runtime trap on the stub. But it PASSES `--no-cache` AND fresh-cache standalone (measured 20/20 + 10/10). So it's cumulative-cache contamination from the ~150 prior tests, triggering the order-sensitive cross-module inherited-field resolution: `copy_parent_fields` (ast_lowering.rs ~7010) RELIES ON \"processing classes in order\" (its own comment ~7014) — parent `BalancedTree` must register fields before child `EnumValueMap` copies them; cumulative cache makes that order non-deterministic. This is an instance of F6 (cached-module cross-module refs stale vs fresh modules). **PITFALLS (burned 2026-06-23):** (1) SINGLE-RUN BISECT IS INVALID here — the flake fooled it into falsely blaming d44c8728 (array-GEP); the same binary both passes and fails. Per [[bugs_test_copy_clone_identity_flaky]] never attribute a flaky cache/exit-138/133 failure without an N≥40 A/B. (2) It is NOT commits 348f9b7b/15d73a7d (fresh-cache passes 20/20 with them; they're TAST/link, not cache-layout). (3) DO NOT \"fix\" it at the resolution site — synthesizing `this.\u003cname\u003e` for an unresolved bare ident in a CLASS instance method (extending the abstract arm at ast_lowering.rs Ident `None` branch ~7613) RESOLVED the compile error but BROKE the cache path: fresh-cache went 20/20 PASS → 20/20 FAIL (the synthesized field access mis-lays-out under caching). Reverted. The real fix is F6 cache-coherence, not name resolution.\n\n**Interim ops:** NO_CACHE=true for benches; scrub `.rayzor` after\nediting nue sources when caches are on. Failure is loud (panic /\nexception / no-listen), never silently wrong numbers.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_blade_mixed_cache_coherence` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}